  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oceans Reporting Engagement Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oceans are threatened by complex economic factors and supply chains with ripple
effects across numerous environmental biomes, communities, and governments. Significant time,
resources, and training are needed to undertake the kind of cross-border and cross-ocean reporting
capable of delivering stories that produce societal and legislative impact and hold relevant powers to
account.This project builds an oceans-reporting initiative with one track of work supporting individual projects of finite scope and duration and a second track supporting year-long full-time investigative fellowships. Grants and fellowships will be distributed globally, with a focus on marginalized communities and developing countries affected
directly by oceans degradation.</narrative>
  </description>
